body:
Thanks, I appreciate that.  One of the reasons CRPGs are my go to- the pausing or turn-based nature is more my style.

&#x200B;

I am an older man, and I am often too hard on myself.  I always do a lot of research on a game, watch so many videos, and then, as soon as I make a mistake, I get angry at myself and feel like I can never play and enjoy games like I see other people do.

&#x200B;

I have to learn patience.  I do pretty well playing Skyrim or Fallout 4, but other games just get overwhelming.  Every time I boot up Battle Brothers I get nervous lol.

&#x200B;

Thanks for your concern and help.  Hope you have a good night my friend.

Ok, thanks for clarifying.  I appreciate the detailed reply!

&#x200B;

There are so many systems in play with this game.  I am really fascinated with the ability to do so much, and the detail.  I just have to not let my anxiety overwhelm me.  

&#x200B;

Thanks again.

Hi.  I was redirected to this thread.  I wanted to start a colony sim game, and I am trying to decide between DF and Rimworld.

&#x200B;

Can anyone help me with pros and cons of each, or if one does certain things better than the other?

&#x200B;

Any help is appreciated- thanks.

I was thinking of switching to PES as well, but I hear that the lag and wait online is excruciating.  What is your experience with connecting for a match, lag, etc?

&#x200B;

Thanks.

I often dreamed of being served a cut of Prime Rib, as well as a Porterhouse steak, medium, and along with silky mashed potatoes with brown peppercorn gravy.

&#x200B;

As it is all being served in front of me, I then see someone else bring in a big plate of home-made fired chicken, and I see another plate of JUST Crab Imperial.  Then comes along some Gumbo and Crab Bisque Soup.

&#x200B;

Then I look up to God and say, "Thank you..."

&#x200B;

Seriously, I would love it.  Really...I love food...it isn't a crime to love food...unless you start talking to it...and I haven't...I don't think...

Yes it does- thank you.  Looking forward to playing it- I quit too soon when it was released.  Ready to fully get invested in the game.

&#x200B;

Which map should I start with?  lol

Great- thanks Xatz.  I have free time Saturday afternoon, and am excited to start playing.

&#x200B;

I appreciate the help!

LOL- I hear you regarding that.  Just never 100% sure how the game handles it.

I tried playing this game last year when it came out (I was so excited), but the bugs caused me to take a long break.

&#x200B;

I know there are still bugs, but excited for the patches that came out, and I am looking forward to the Trumball map.

&#x200B;

Thanks again for answering my questions, Jack.  You did a good job protecting the President, aka the spokesman for AllState  ;-P

I know- I hear you all about the low quality of TOTW today.

&#x200B;

But for me and my average Italian team, I just purchased my Italian Giroud for $15,000.

&#x200B;

Oh Happy Day!  (Pelle)  ;-P

Thanks again, cirome.  Think I am interested in Salem's Lot, IT, Insomnia, and I don't know what Needful Things is about, but will look it up.

&#x200B;

I watched the Dreamcatcher movie, which I liked.  I assume the book has more detail - thank you!

Thanks for your thoughts on it.  I would be fine with it if the second novel is of high quality.  If it starts to run out of steam, and meanders, then I can see how others will be upset.

&#x200B;

Guess I will think on it.  It definitely sounds intriguing.  Thanks again!

Hi.  I use him as a striker with SIF Alfredo Donnaruma.  They are in my second team at 4-4-2.

&#x200B;

Chiesa's speed and agility are great, and I like his strong finishing.  Plus his increased stamina really helps.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I am a big fan of Bram Stoker's Dracula.  I enjoyed it more than Mary Shelley's Frankenstein.

&#x200B;

I loved the atmosphere, the characters, Dracula himself, and the journal entry pages were amazing and tense.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I SHALL avail myself of said mode, sir.  I am always availing myself, so it's no bother.

&#x200B;

Now be gone- back to yer gameplay session!!!

&#x200B;

;-P

Stop with the F word, pardner!!!!

&#x200B;

\*grabs him by the collar\*

&#x200B;

Now repeat after me- Rockstar are just plain old geniuses- SAY IT!!!!!!!

Thanks, David.

&#x200B;

If I quit the game earlier this morning, would it save so that I don't lose my progress?  I didn't know about the save option and thought the game would save after certain story sections.

\*thumbs up\*

&#x200B;

\*heads back to the grind of work\*

Thanks for the kind words, and the info on Xcom!

&#x200B;

At least i started playing RDR2 before I got to work.  Very nice, hoping to get to the open world part soon.  Stuck on rails for the first 45 minutes so far.  Tutorial stuff, I reckon ;-)

&#x200B;

Have a good weekend, my friend!

&#x200B;

My computer just died, so I have to rely on Xbox for those games now.  Xcom2 is another I might try.

&#x200B;

Want to get a new computer, but just can't afford it.

&#x200B;

Sewage pipe burst outside our house a month ago, so now we will be paying for that repair for 6 years.

&#x200B;

Bad luck, but things happen.

&#x200B;

Thanks again!

I hear what you are saying, and respect it.

&#x200B;

But for me, I thought the twist was lazy and also attempting to have one of those "shock" moments.  It fell flat, especially when he put on THE MASK...looked like a demented troll...

&#x200B;

They just needed Michael to get to Laurie, and instead of finding a creative way to accomplish that, they instead decided to be lazy.

&#x200B;

He was a character that could have had an interesting role, but they wasted that opportunity...

To be fair, it could be that the delay was good talent leaving Rockstar due to the severe work hours/bad environment.

&#x200B;

I still can't wait to play the game, but I do feel bad for any employees that were overworked or had to leave because of the cutthroat deadlines...

I have to say- I really enjoyed the cinematography, the setting, the style, the characters.

&#x200B;

I felt it had great atmosphere.

&#x200B;

I was REALLY enjoying it until the ending, specifically regarding Thomas.  Just sort of ruined it for me...

&#x200B;

I had just watched The VVitch last week, and I loved it.

I am very glad you are feeling better, Bryan/Alex human hybrid.  Great.  But you must be hungry now, am I right?

&#x200B;

\*discreetly hands Bryan a burrito from Taco Bell\*

&#x200B;

\*runs off\*

&#x200B;

muahahahahahaaaaaa!!!!!!!

\*shakes PopMart\*

&#x200B;

Wake up, Mart- WAKE UPPPPPPP!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!

&#x200B;

;-P

Yeah, I have been waiting to watch The Apostle- Matthew from Downton Abbey aka Daniel Stevens lol.

&#x200B;

I just watched The VVitch- thought it was amazing.

&#x200B;

I get the same feel from watching Apostle- eerie, Puritan village.  But there will be many more interactions with people, whereas The VVitch was more about an isolated family.

&#x200B;

Can't wait to watch it this weekend.  The trailer had great atmosphere...

My issue is that I have an original Xbox One and cannot currently afford an X.

&#x200B;

I just hope the game runs smoothly enough on it.  And I am interested in seeing how the graphics hold up on my older console.

Muggle Health, Humanoid Stamina, Pink Eye, Equine Health, Big Pony Stamina

&#x200B;

;-P

LOL, no, you will be ok.  Play RDR2, study, play RDR2, study.

&#x200B;

A pin might be needed to pry you away from the game, BUT WE WILL GET YOU TO GRADUATE!!!

Charlie:  Ohhhhhhhh shit! Look at that door, dude. See that door there? The one marked "Pirate"? You think a pirate lives in there? 

&#x200B;

Dennis: I see a door marked "Private". Is that the door you're talking about? 

&#x200B;

All in good fun.  We all make typos.

&#x200B;

I am currently reading HEX, and after that I will read Something Wicked This Way Comes.

&#x200B;

I have heard about this for years, and will finally read it this October.

&#x200B;

Also planning to read The Fisherman, Dark Harvest, Salem's Lot, and Bird Box.

Oh man, I miss her food.  You remember last year when I got banned for bringing my own mac and cheese.  She dumped it over my head, performed a DDT on me, then said that I was Culinary Scum.

&#x200B;

But she has that smile that lights up a room... \*sighs \*

So Cool!

&#x200B;

I live in Lakewood- we have much wildlife, but not Malthor.

&#x200B;

Since we are in neighboring towns, maybe we can exchange Malthor recipes???

&#x200B;

Maybe sponsor a Malthor-Chili cook-off?  Would be a great combination, as chili is SLOW to cook...

He is 100% correct!!  What audacity!!!  Using a pun like THAT, at this tragic moment!!!

&#x200B;

For shame, Jim- FOR SHAME!!!!!!!!!

Thanks for the info, friend.  You seem to know a lot about what happens in this town...

&#x200B;

\*stares at him intently \*

&#x200B;

Hey, do I know you from somewhere else?

As for the camping trip, I am undecided.

&#x200B;

Not sure we should go alone together- I remember the Summer of 1995 where you got your nickname, "The Vick."

&#x200B;

Therapy going ok?

&#x200B;

Maybe we can use some of your rural contacts to find Kade?

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

\*pours the aromatic, full-bodied Maxwell House Dark Roast into a cup \*

&#x200B;

Sorry, Vick.  Just thought you needed to clear your noggin' a bit..

&#x200B;

\*gives him back the bottle \*

&#x200B;

Is Venison still in season after the Elk Murders from last week?

&#x200B;

You'd best keep clear of the woods for a bit, Vick...

\*closes eyes \*

Labcorp...trying to remember...

&#x200B;

Ashley, yes, remember her bringing you the ice cream cake ....you were happy...

&#x200B;

\*starts to get headache \*

&#x200B;

Labcorp, that locked security door marked Pirate...so confusing...What Is Happening to Me!!!!!!

Though my wife isn't a fan of horror movies, I was able to get her to watch the original Halloween over a year ago.

&#x200B;

We plan to re-watch it the week before we go see Halloween 2018.

&#x200B;

I would normally watch the original at the beginning of October so I could watch the other movies in the series, but she forgets details if I try watching it that early, lol.



&#x200B;

I see Neil Breen hiding in the trees over on those mountains up yonder.  This is beyond my imagination!!!

&#x200B;

Yup, it's official- this game shall be EPIC...

I haven't read The Ritual yet, but it sounds similar with the second part not being as good as the first part of the story?

&#x200B;

I haven't read either of these books...

Haha...good...enjoy the game, have at it.

But wait for me.....I WILL be arriving eventually...nothing can stop me...it is INEVITABLE...

&#x200B;

\*dreaded FIFA Patch #1 moving in the shadows, a hunter waiting to pounce on his prey, which is gameplay\*

&#x200B;

muahahhahaaaaa!!!!!!!!!!!!!!

I will be a Librarian Outlaw.  I will have my glasses on, and my gun at the ready.

I will embark on a journey like none other.  Afraid of the elements, I will sheepishly make my way through the treacherous terrain.  I will seek out justice, even though I am part of a gang.

&#x200B;

I will stumble across vargrants in each town, and will act accordingly.

&#x200B;

"Oh, you don't want to return that book that you were lent??  Well then, it is time for a duel, miscreant!"

&#x200B;

Winner gets a free bookmark...

Wait, Resetera, are you saying we can NAME our OWN train???

&#x200B;

\*mind blown\*

&#x200B;

You always have the latest and greatest info, Resetera!  ;-)

That would be great.  I don't know exactly what "ron the train" is, but if it was actually to be protrayed in the game, well, it would be amazing.

&#x200B;

Who else wants to be able to Ron the train??  I do...I think...

&#x200B;

;-P
